    "deletions": 29,
    "body": "## Summary\n\nBind the installed Rust collector to existing generic configuration and authenticated Core requests. Delivery preflight checks exact installed payloads, observed Core/tool/ABI identities, receipt and capture context before a complete retained-binary native re-export. Owner projection emits exact measurement facts; released Core continues to decide policy. No Rust-specific Core dispatch or fallback is introduced.\n\nCompletes the locally evidenced GH-230 tasks P6.1–P6.2 and P7.1–P7.3 under parent #225. Predecessor #229 was accepted and PR #235 merged; this branch incorporates main `ee544690662645806cda7dd4cd2c9192566f7929`. P8, required hosted CI and controller acceptance remain pending.\n\nFresh clean-container fixture capture, matching full native re-exports and actual official Core v0.4.0 decisions are retained, including unsupported capability states, stale context, malformed output, wrong tools, relocation and missing owners. Independent exec traces establish producer counts. The successful measurement produces the expected Core policy failure, without a measurement error. The distributed Core SHA-256 is `8e3df8303ca8f650d4ef768b29cfefb60ca115122a47b116245cc19e4649bbdd`.\n\nEvidence and exact supported tuple: [acceptance](https://github.com/musutrade/Harness-Gate/blob/9b53a47fa40706eaecb0f3b768749f4540841cbb/docs/quality/gh-230/acceptance.md), [validation](https://github.com/musutrade/Harness-Gate/blob/9b53a47fa40706eaecb0f3b768749f4540841cbb/docs/quality/gh-230/final-validation.md), [OpenSpec design](https://github.com/musutrade/Harness-Gate/blob/9b53a47fa40706eaecb0f3b768749f4540841cbb/openspec/changes/package-official-rust-collector-for-independent-delivery/design.md), [tasks](https://github.com/musutrade/Harness-Gate/blob/9b53a47fa40706eaecb0f3b768749f4540841cbb/openspec/changes/package-official-rust-collector-for-independent-delivery/tasks.md), and [binding schema](https://github.com/musutrade/Harness-Gate/blob/9b53a47fa40706eaecb0f3b768749f4540841cbb/tools/quality/schema/rust-project-collector-binding.schema.json). Original successful and failed capture bytes remain durable. Large archives use numbered binary parts with SHA-256 manifests and reconstruction commands because shell Git transport is unavailable and large API blob uploads time out.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `cargo nextest run --manifest-path tools/harness-gate/Cargo.toml --locked` — 392 passed, zero skips.\n- [x] `cargo fmt --manifest-path tools/harness-gate/Cargo.toml -- --check` — passed.\n- [x] `cargo clippy --manifest-path tools/harness-gate/Cargo.toml --all-targets -- -D warnings` — passed.\n- [x] `python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/quality/tests -v` — 439 passed, zero skips, including provisioned native integration with distributed Core v0.4.0.\n- [x] `python3 -m unittest discover -s tools/release/tests -v` — 42 passed.\n- [x] `python3 tools/quality/docs_consistency.py --output target/quality/docs-consistency.json` — passed.\n- [x] `OPENSPEC_TELEMETRY=0 openspec validate package-official-rust-collector-for-independent-delivery --strict --no-interactive` — passed.\n- [x] Git diff whitespace check, evidence reconstruction hashes, relevant documentation/schema/OpenSpec updates — passed.\n\n`harness-gate config check` and `harness-gate verify --profile ci --all` are not applicable: this source checkout has no project-local `.harness-gate/flow.toml` declaring `ci`. No configuration was invented. The template's separate `cargo test` and all-features Clippy commands are not claimed as locally run; the exact issue-required commands above were run. Required CI belongs to the controller.\n\nValidation logs retain genuine initial failures and corrections, including Git fixture isolation, the new B-class inventory row, and documentation links. Frozen C/D policy semantics remain unchanged. Builds, temporary paths and captures stayed in this assigned workspace.\n\nSubmission-only failures: shell `git push -u origin symphony/GH-230` could not connect to GitHub; the 12 MB Git blob API request timed out. Smaller immutable blob uploads succeeded. An amend attempted while staging was still running reported `index.lock`; waiting for staging resolved it. Git initially treated some gzip fragments as text and reported whitespace; the committed `.gitattributes` marks those fragments binary, and the final full-change diff check passed. These transport corrections do not alter the reconstructed archive bytes or native results.\n\n## Safety and rollback\n\nThe frozen evidence covers the observed Linux x86_64 GNU/glibc 2.43 fixture combination with private Python 3.14.4, rustc 1.97.1 and LLVM 22.1.6. It certifies clean-container execution on that host; it does not certify fresh-VM installation, additional platforms or Arc-Admin. The shipping compatibility matrix remains empty pending separately approved release evidence. Synthetic candidate distribution eligibility/signing tests package installation and does not authorize publication or authenticate runtime captures.\n\nMeasured package size is 1,623,490,560 bytes. Fresh-directory cold setup took 38.401654 s; warm selection took 16.716137 s. Sampled setup peak allocated disk was 3,249,242,112 bytes. OS caches were not flushed and sampled peaks are not universal performance guarantees. Native capture/re-export timings and exact launch counts are in the retained receipts.\n\nRequiredness, thresholds, baseline/lineage, debt/ratchet, CRAP/coverage and final outcomes remain owned by released Core. Relocation does not establish series equivalence. Rollback is to revert this integration and its package payload additions; there is no policy/release fallback, baseline reset or automatic project enablement. No tags, release publication, Arc-Admin writes, business-test changes or #215 acceptance are included.\n\nController handoff: submitted for required CI and review. Please use the existing lifecycle for acceptance, merge and issue completion; #231 remains the already-authorized successor after acceptance and merge.\n\nThe GitHub API also returned HTTP 422 with a timeout when assembling all 232 tree entries in one request. Incremental tree assembly was used, with the final tree and commit checked against local Git object hashes before publishing the branch.\n",
